    Release signing + toolchain: upload keystore support, vendored lucide_icons
    
    - build.gradle.kts: release builds sign with the upload keystore when
      android/key.properties exists (git-ignored, machine-local), falling
      back to the debug keystore otherwise. Previously release ALWAYS signed
      CN=Android Debug (audit P0-8), which Play Console rejects. The upload
      keystore lives outside the repo; losing it loses update rights.
    - Version 1.0.0+10 -> 1.0.0+11 (previous Play upload may hold code 10).
    - Toolchain floor raised to build with Flutter 3.47: Gradle wrapper
      8.12 -> 8.14.3, AGP 8.9.1 -> 8.11.1, Kotlin 2.1.0 -> 2.2.20, plus two
      gradle.properties flags added by the Flutter migrator. All remain
      compatible with the pinned Flutter 3.35.6.
    - lucide_icons 0.257.0 (abandoned upstream) subclasses IconData, which
      is a final class in newer Flutter - no longer compiles. Vendored a
      patched copy under third_party/lucide_icons (all 1191 icons as plain
      IconData, same font; LICENSE + font asset included) wired via
      dependency_overrides. Call sites unchanged; works on 3.35 and 3.47.
    - analysis_options.yaml: exclude build/ and platform dirs from analyze.
    - pubspec.lock + generated plugin registrants regenerated by 3.47.
    
    flutter test: 33/33 with these changes.
    
